 dna  methylation from sequence and across  species  these across species models are  competitive to models trained only  within species at least within the mds  firms  and the tcp family mates we saw are  entirely global importance to the across  species of accessibility walls  but for the methylation models it is ap2  and erf  and i'm also happy to report that there  is a preprint available that shows what  i've discussed here and also more on  bioarchive  um i've uploaded the data in the models  to xeno which are linked to the  pre-print  and there's code on github which  includes instructions for making your  own progressions in your favorite  species if you'd like  and finally i'd like to acknowledge uh  my community and eric for their guidance  on my co-authors for all the workfields  in making this paper happen  particularly pete he called those extra  dipot uh unlimited reasons for him and  as well as the [ __ ] with that for all  their feedback and the funding sources  and  high performance computing departments  and without it behind  so i asked do you have better hp on  rhodopsis and rice compared with maize  and other species  does this mean the genome complexity of  playing a role yeah that's a great  question i didn't show it here  but i do notice  um a trend so as genome size increases  my performance  increases and what this boils down to is  that the model um i also show this it  makes more false positive mistakes than  it does  so  what i mean by false positive is  the model calls it open but the data is  labeled as closed  and so in these larger genomes that  effect is a lot more pronounced and so i  get  less of an accuracy in those species um  there's a number of reasons why i think  this is the case uh first  the ataxi in the angiosperms was called  very conservatively  but there's a potential that the model  is calling things that are actually open  in vivo but just weren't able to be  captured in the  concerned certainly calling sort of  constraints um  yeah there's also a number of other  reasons but i hope that answers your  question  um do you have a sense of how additive  these motif effects tend to be they  should be fairly active um basically  it's been shown so what's more important  though actually is the businesses  haven't shown the additive to an extent  that they can  sort of interact with each other at the  regulatory site but what's more  important is that they're trying to be  redundant so if you start deleting these  motifs it doesn't necessarily mean that  expression will be impacted and so  that's also a few points  this has been a production of cornell  university on the web at cornell.edu

